| Interval | $P$ at left | $P$ at right |
|---|---|---|
| $(0.05,\, 0.1)$ | $P(0.05) \approx -0.0188 < 0$ | $P(0.1) \approx 0.0379 > 0$ |
| $(0.1,\, 0.2)$ | $P(0.1) \approx 0.0379 > 0$ | $P(0.2) = -928/625 < 0$ |
| $(0.5,\, 0.8)$ | $P(0.5) = -4.46875 < 0$ | $P(0.8) \approx 11.461 > 0$ |
| $(1.8,\, 1.9)$ | $P(1.8) \approx 28.62 > 0$ | $P(1.9) \approx -1.97 < 0$ |
| $(4,\, 5)$ | $P(4) = -1189 < 0$ | $P(5) = 7904 > 0$ |

These five disjoint intervals each contain a real root, so $P$ has **at least** $5$ distinct positive real roots. Since $\deg P = 5$, it has **exactly** $5$ real roots, all positive (and no complex roots).

**Applying Vieta's formula.** The sum of all roots of $P(t) = 35t^5 - 245t^4 + \cdots$ equals $-(-245)/35 = 7$. Since all five roots are real and positive, the sum of the positive real roots is $7$.

Therefore

$$\sum_{x \in S} x^2 = 7.$$

